      "time": 1780168275.305968,
      "metadata": {
        "tool_calls": [
          {
            "kind": "edit",
            "title": "Creating ...te/b2b3476e-5c60-40ee-bba7-6e719d7ee678/plan.md",
            "raw_input": {
              "path": "/Users/matthewgold/.copilot/session-state/b2b3476e-5c60-40ee-bba7-6e719d7ee678/plan.md",
              "file_text": "# Psychiatric Rehospitalization Data Analysis Plan\n\n## Problem Statement\nAnalyze retrospective chart data on psychiatric rehospitalization in school-aged children. The dataset contains 2,652 patient records with ICD-10 codes scattered across three diagnosis columns (VisitDiags, NonSuicidialDiags, ChronicDiags). To begin meaningful analysis, we need to:\n1. Map 1,863 unique ICD-10 codes to clinical diagnosis names\n2. Link psychiatric diagnoses to their DSM-5 TR equivalents where applicable\n3. Create a reference table for subsequent trend and association analysis\n\n## Proposed Approach\n- Build an ICD-10 to DSM-5 TR diagnosis reference using automated lookup (ICD-10-CM official mappings + clinical resources)\n- Focus on psychiatric codes (F-codes) as primary clinical indicators\n- Tag non-psychiatric codes (comorbid conditions) for potential confounding/protective factor analysis\n- Create a cleaned dataset with diagnosis names for exploratory analysis\n- Enable systematic comparison of visit diagnoses vs. chronic diagnoses vs. self-injury-related codes\n\n## Deliverables\n1. **ICD Reference Table**: ICD-10 code \u2192 diagnosis name \u2192 DSM-5 TR category/equivalent\n2. **Annotated Dataset**: Original data with diagnosis names joined to the three ICD columns\n3. **Diagnostic Summary**: Frequency of diagnoses by type and association with readmission\n4. **Analysis-Ready Dataset**: Clean CSV for trend/association analysis\n\n## Implementation Steps\n1. Query official ICD-10-CM to DSM-5 TR mapping resources\n2. Create reference lookup tables in Python\n3. Parse and normalize the ICD codes from the three diagnosis columns\n4. Merge reference data with patient records\n5. Generate summary statistics and preliminary associations\n6. Export analysis-ready dataset\n"
            },
            "locations": [
              "/Users/matthewgold/.copilot/session-state/b2b3476e-5c60-40ee-bba7-6e719d7ee678/plan.md"
            ],
            "raw_output": {
              "detailedContent": "\ndiff --git a/Users/matthewgold/.copilot/session-state/b2b3476e-5c60-40ee-bba7-6e719d7ee678/plan.md b/Users/matthewgold/.copilot/session-state/b2b3476e-5c60-40ee-bba7-6e719d7ee678/plan.md\ncreate file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..0000000\n--- a/dev/null\n+++ b/Users/matthewgold/.copilot/session-state/b2b3476e-5c60-40ee-bba7-6e719d7ee678/plan.md\n@@ -1,0 +1,29 @@\n+# Psychiatric Rehospitalization Data Analysis Plan\n+\n+## Problem Statement\n+Analyze retrospective chart data on psychiatric rehospitalization in school-aged children. The dataset contains 2,652 patient records with ICD-10 codes scattered across three diagnosis columns (VisitDiags, NonSuicidialDiags, ChronicDiags). To begin meaningful analysis, we need to:\n+1. Map 1,863 unique ICD-10 codes to clinical diagnosis names\n+2. Link psychiatric diagnoses to their DSM-5 TR equivalents where applicable\n+3. Create a reference table for subsequent trend and association analysis\n+\n+## Proposed Approach\n+- Build an ICD-10 to DSM-5 TR diagnosis reference using automated lookup (ICD-10-CM official mappings + clinical resources)\n+- Focus on psychiatric codes (F-codes) as primary clinical indicators\n+- Tag non-psychiatric codes (comorbid conditions) for potential confounding/protective factor analysis\n+- Create a cleaned dataset with diagnosis names for exploratory analysis\n+- Enable systematic comparison of visit diagnoses vs. chronic diagnoses vs. self-injury-related codes\n+\n+## Deliverables\n+1. **ICD Reference Table**: ICD-10 code \u2192 diagnosis name \u2192 DSM-5 TR category/equivalent\n+2. **Annotated Dataset**: Original data with diagnosis names joined to the three ICD columns\n+3. **Diagnostic Summary**: Frequency of diagnoses by type and association with readmission\n+4. **Analysis-Ready Dataset**: Clean CSV for trend/association analysis\n+\n+## Implementation Steps\n+1. Query official ICD-10-CM to DSM-5 TR mapping resources\n+2. Create reference lookup tables in Python\n+3. Parse and normalize the ICD codes from the three diagnosis columns\n+4. Merge reference data with patient records\n+5. Generate summary statistics and preliminary associations\n+6. Export analysis-ready dataset\n+\n",
