              "description": "Create comprehensive analysis summary",
              "command": "cd /Users/matthewgold/code/jupyter_projects && source venv/bin/activate && python3 << 'EOFPY'\nimport pandas as pd\n\n# Load all analysis files\nannotated = pd.read_csv('annotated_psychiatric_data.csv')\ndiag_long = pd.read_csv('diagnoses_long_form.csv')\nref_table = pd.read_csv('ICD10_to_DSM5_Reference.csv')\ndsm5_summary = pd.read_csv('DSM5_Category_Summary.csv', index_col=0)\ndsm5_readmit = pd.read_csv('DSM5_Readmission_Analysis.csv', index_col=0)\n\n# Create comprehensive summary\nsummary = f\"\"\"PSYCHIATRIC REHOSPITALIZATION DATA ANALYSIS\nICD-10 to DSM-5 TR MAPPING & READMISSION TRENDS\n===============================================\n\nDATASET OVERVIEW\n================\nSource: GD1854RVSD Psychiatric Rehospitalization in School-Aged Children\nTotal Records: {len(annotated)} patient admissions\nDate Range: 2017-2019\nGeographic: Arizona (AHCCCS, major commercial insurers)\n\nDIAGNOSTIC CODING ANALYSIS\n===========================\nTotal ICD-10 Codes in Dataset: {len(ref_table)}\nTotal Diagnosis Records (long form): {len(diag_long)}\n\nDiagnosis Distribution by Type:\n  - Visit Diagnoses: {(diag_long['diagnosis_type'] == 'Visit').sum():,} records\n  - NSSI-Related Diagnoses: {(diag_long['diagnosis_type'] == 'NSSI').sum():,} records\n  - Chronic Comorbid Diagnoses: {(diag_long['diagnosis_type'] == 'Chronic').sum():,} records\n\nDSM-5 TR Mapping Coverage:\n  - DSM-5 Mapped Diagnoses: {diag_long['dsm5_category'].notna().sum():,} records ({100*diag_long['dsm5_category'].notna().mean():.1f}%)\n  - Psychiatric Categories Identified: {diag_long['dsm5_category'].nunique()}\n  - Medical/Other Categories: {diag_long['icd_category'].nunique()}\n\nMOST COMMON DIAGNOSES (TOP 15)\n==============================\n{ref_table[ref_table['Frequency_in_Dataset'] > 0][['ICD_10_Code', 'Diagnosis_Name', 'DSM5_Category', 'Frequency_in_Dataset']].head(15).to_string(index=False)}\n\nTOP DSM-5 DIAGNOSTIC CATEGORIES\n================================\nBy Prevalence (Unique Patients):\n{dsm5_summary.sort_values('Unique_Patients', ascending=False).head(10).to_string()}\n\nREADMISSION ANALYSIS\n====================\nOverall Statistics:\n  - Patients with Readmissions: {(annotated['Readmissions'] > 0).sum():,}/{len(annotated)} ({100*(annotated['Readmissions'] > 0).mean():.1f}%)\n  - Total Readmissions: {annotated['Readmissions'].sum():,}\n  - Mean Readmissions per Patient: {annotated['Readmissions'].mean():.2f}\n\nHighest Readmission Risk Diagnoses:\n{dsm5_readmit[['Readmitted_Count', 'Unique_Patients', 'Readmission_Rate_%']].head(10).to_string()}\n\nKEY CLINICAL INSIGHTS\n=====================\n1. SUICIDAL IDEATION (R45.851) is the single most common diagnosis:\n   - 2,968 occurrences (29.2% readmission rate)\n   - Documented in NSSI column indicating self-injury context\n   \n2. NEURODEVELOPMENTAL DISORDERS are highly represented:\n   - ADHD: 2,333 occurrences (18.4% readmission rate)\n   - Autism Spectrum Disorder: 794 occurrences (19.9% readmission rate)\n   - Conduct Disorder: 696 occurrences (19.8% readmission rate)\n   \n3. INTERNALIZING DISORDERS prevalent:\n   - Depressive Disorders: 3,182 occurrences (20.2% readmission rate)\n   - Anxiety Disorders: 1,980 occurrences (18.5% readmission rate)\n   - PTSD/Trauma-Related: 2,572 occurrences (19.7% readmission rate)\n\n4. HIGH-RISK DIAGNOSTIC GROUPS (>25% readmission rate):\n   - Neurocognitive Disorders (33.3%)\n   - Non-Suicidal Self-Injury Behavior (29.2%)\n   - Other Neurodevelopmental Disorders (27.7%)\n   - Mental Disorders Due to Medical Condition (27.3%)\n\nDELIVERABLES CREATED\n====================\n1. ICD10_to_DSM5_Reference.csv\n   Complete mapping of all 1,863 ICD-10 codes in dataset to:\n   - Diagnosis name\n   - ICD-10 category\n   - DSM-5 TR category (where applicable)\n   - DSM-5 code\n   - Frequency in dataset\n\n2. DSM5_Category_Summary.csv\n   Prevalence statistics for 31 DSM-5 diagnostic categories\n   - Unique patients per category\n   - Total occurrences\n   - Useful for epidemiologic analysis\n\n3. DSM5_Readmission_Analysis.csv\n   Risk stratification by psychiatric diagnosis\n   - Readmitted counts and rates\n   - Identifies high-risk diagnostic groups\n   - Actionable for clinical intervention prioritization\n\n4. annotated_psychiatric_data.csv\n   Original dataset enhanced with:\n   - Diagnosis names for all three ICD columns\n   - DSM-5 category assignments\n   - DSM-5 mapping counts\n   - Ready for multivariate analysis\n\n5. diagnoses_long_form.csv\n   27,884 diagnosis records for granular analysis:\n   - One row per diagnosis per patient\n   - Includes diagnosis type (Visit/NSSI/Chronic)\n   - DSM-5 category for systematic grouping\n   - Ideal for trend analysis and ML applications\n\nNEXT STEPS FOR ANALYSIS\n=======================\n1. Temporal trends: Track diagnostic patterns across admission dates\n2. Comorbidity analysis: Identify co-occurring diagnostic combinations\n3. Sociodemographic patterns: Age/gender/insurance associations\n4. Readmission prediction: Use diagnostic combinations as features\n5. Treatment response analysis: Link diagnoses to discharge outcomes\n\nFILES AVAILABLE IN PROJECT DIRECTORY\n=====================================\nAll analysis files are in: /Users/matthewgold/code/jupyter_projects/\n\nReference data (for repeated use):\n  - comprehensive_icd_ref.pkl (Python pickle - all ICD mappings)\n\nAnalysis-ready datasets:\n  - annotated_psychiatric_data.csv (wide format, patient-level)\n  - diagnoses_long_form.csv (long format, diagnosis-level)\n  - ICD10_to_DSM5_Reference.csv (reference table)\n  - DSM5_Category_Summary.csv (category statistics)\n  - DSM5_Readmission_Analysis.csv (readmission risk analysis)\n\n\"\"\"\n\nprint(summary)\n\n# Save summary\nwith open('ANALYSIS_SUMMARY.txt', 'w') as f:\n    f.write(summary)\n\nprint(\"\\n\u2713 Summary saved to ANALYSIS_SUMMARY.txt\")\nEOFPY\n"
            },
