            "raw_output": {
              "content": "{\"type\":\"output_text\",\"text\":{\"value\":\"Certainly! Here's a breakdown of the requested **ICD-10-CM codes** and their descriptions for the categories provided:\\n\\n---\\n\\n### **F90: Attention-deficit hyperactivity disorders (ADHD)**\\n- **F90.0** - Attention-deficit hyperactivity disorder, predominantly inattentive type  \\n- **F90.1** - Attention-deficit hyperactivity disorder, predominantly hyperactive-impulsive type  \\n- **F90.2** - Attention-deficit hyperactivity disorder, combined type  \\n- **F90.8** - Other attention-deficit hyperactivity disorders  \\n- **F90.9** - Attention-deficit hyperactivity disorder, unspecified type\\n\\n---\\n\\n### **F91: Conduct disorders**\\n- **F91.0** - Conduct disorder confined to family context  \\n- **F91.1** - Conduct disorder, childhood-onset type  \\n- **F91.2** - Conduct disorder, adolescent-onset type  \\n- **F91.3** - Oppositional defiant disorder  \\n- **F91.8** - Other conduct disorders  \\n- **F91.9** - Conduct disorder, unspecified\\n\\n---\\n\\n### **F32: Major depressive disorder, single episode**\\n- **F32.0** - Major depressive disorder, single episode, mild  \\n- **F32.1** - Major depressive disorder, single episode, moderate  \\n- **F32.2** - Major depressive disorder, single episode, severe without psychotic features  \\n- **F32.3** - Major depressive disorder, single episode, severe with psychotic symptoms  \\n- **F32.4** - Major depressive disorder, single episode, in partial remission  \\n- **F32.5** - Major depressive disorder, single episode, in full remission  \\n- **F32.8** - Other depressive episodes  \\n- **F32.9** - Major depressive disorder, single episode, unspecified\\n\\n---\\n\\n### **F33: Major depressive disorder, recurrent**\\n- **F33.0** - Major depressive disorder, recurrent, mild  \\n- **F33.1** - Major depressive disorder, recurrent, moderate  \\n- **F33.2** - Major depressive disorder, recurrent, severe without psychotic features  \\n- **F33.3** - Major depressive disorder, recurrent, severe with psychotic symptoms  \\n- **F33.40** - Major depressive disorder, recurrent, in remission, unspecified  \\n- **F33.41** - Major depressive disorder, recurrent, in partial remission  \\n- **F33.42** - Major depressive disorder, recurrent, in full remission  \\n- **F33.8** - Other recurrent depressive disorders  \\n- **F33.9** - Major depressive disorder, recurrent, unspecified\\n\\n---\\n\\n### **F84: Pervasive developmental disorders (including Autism Spectrum Disorders)**\\n- **F84.0** - Autistic disorder  \\n- **F84.2** - Rett's syndrome  \\n- **F84.3** - Other childhood disintegrative disorder  \\n- **F84.5** - Asperger's syndrome  \\n- **F84.8** - Other pervasive developmental disorders  \\n- **F84.9** - Pervasive developmental disorder, unspecified\\n\\n---\\n\\n### **Common ICD-10-CM Codes for Anxiety and Depression**\\n\\n#### **Anxiety Disorders (commonly F41)**\\n- **F41.0** - Panic disorder [episodic paroxysmal anxiety]  \\n- **F41.1** - Generalized anxiety disorder  \\n- **F41.3** - Other mixed anxiety disorders  \\n- **F41.8** - Other specified anxiety disorders  \\n- **F41.9** - Anxiety disorder, unspecified\\n\\n#### **Depression (also covered above in F32 and F33)**\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Note:**  \\n- **ADHD** is under F90.\\n- **Conduct Disorders (including Oppositional Defiant Disorder)** are under F91.\\n- **Major Depression** (single and recurrent) under F32 & F33.\\n- **Autism Spectrum Disorders** under F84.\\n- **Anxiety Disorders** most commonly coded under F41.\\n\\nIf you need the official, full, or the most up-to-date descriptions (as the ICD-10-CM is updated annually), you can refer to the [CDC's ICD-10-CM code lookup tool](https://icd10cmtool.cdc.gov/) or official codebooks. Let me know if you need additional codes or details for specific disorders!\",\"annotations\":null},\"bing_searches\":null,\"annotations\":null}",
              "contents": [
                {
                  "text": "{\n  \"type\": \"output_text\",\n  \"text\": {\n    \"value\": \"Certainly! Here's a breakdown of the requested **ICD-10-CM codes** and their descriptions for the categories provided:\\n\\n---\\n\\n### **F90: Attention-deficit hyperactivity disorders (ADHD)**\\n- **F90.0** - Attention-deficit hyperactivity disorder, predominantly inattentive type  \\n- **F90.1** - Attention-deficit hyperactivity disorder, predominantly hyperactive-impulsive type  \\n- **F90.2** - Attention-deficit hyperactivity disorder, combined type  \\n- **F90.8** - Other attention-deficit hyperactivity disorders  \\n- **F90.9** - Attention-deficit hyperactivity disorder, unspecified type\\n\\n---\\n\\n### **F91: Conduct disorders**\\n- **F91.0** - Conduct disorder confined to family context  \\n- **F91.1** - Conduct disorder, childhood-onset type  \\n- **F91.2** - Conduct disorder, adolescent-onset type  \\n- **F91.3** - Oppositional defiant disorder  \\n- **F91.8** - Other conduct disorders  \\n- **F91.9** - Conduct disorder, unspecified\\n\\n---\\n\\n### **F32: Major depressive disorder, single episode**\\n- **F32.0** - Major depressive disorder, single episode, mild  \\n- **F32.1** - Major depressive disorder, single episode, moderate  \\n- **F32.2** - Major depressive disorder, single episode, severe without psychotic features  \\n- **F32.3** - Major depressive disorder, single episode, severe with psychotic symptoms  \\n- **F32.4** - Major depressive disorder, single episode, in partial remission  \\n- **F32.5** - Major depressive disorder, single episode, in full remission  \\n- **F32.8** - Other depressive episodes  \\n- **F32.9** - Major depressive disorder, single episode, unspecified\\n\\n---\\n\\n### **F33: Major depressive disorder, recurrent**\\n- **F33.0** - Major depressive disorder, recurrent, mild  \\n- **F33.1** - Major depressive disorder, recurrent, moderate  \\n- **F33.2** - Major depressive disorder, recurrent, severe without psychotic features  \\n- **F33.3** - Major depressive disorder, recurrent, severe with psychotic symptoms  \\n- **F33.40** - Major depressive disorder, recurrent, in remission, unspecified  \\n- **F33.41** - Major depressive disorder, recurrent, in partial remission  \\n- **F33.42** - Major depressive disorder, recurrent, in full remission  \\n- **F33.8** - Other recurrent depressive disorders  \\n- **F33.9** - Major depressive disorder, recurrent, unspecified\\n\\n---\\n\\n### **F84: Pervasive developmental disorders (including Autism Spectrum Disorders)**\\n- **F84.0** - Autistic disorder  \\n- **F84.2** - Rett's syndrome  \\n- **F84.3** - Other childhood disintegrative disorder  \\n- **F84.5** - Asperger's syndrome  \\n- **F84.8** - Other pervasive developmental disorders  \\n- **F84.9** - Pervasive developmental disorder, unspecified\\n\\n---\\n\\n### **Common ICD-10-CM Codes for Anxiety and Depression**\\n\\n#### **Anxiety Disorders (commonly F41)**\\n- **F41.0** - Panic disorder [episodic paroxysmal anxiety]  \\n- **F41.1** - Generalized anxiety disorder  \\n- **F41.3** - Other mixed anxiety disorders  \\n- **F41.8** - Other specified anxiety disorders  \\n- **F41.9** - Anxiety disorder, unspecified\\n\\n#### **Depression (also covered above in F32 and F33)**\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Note:**  \\n- **ADHD** is under F90.\\n- **Conduct Disorders (including Oppositional Defiant Disorder)** are under F91.\\n- **Major Depression** (single and recurrent) under F32 \\u0026 F33.\\n- **Autism Spectrum Disorders** under F84.\\n- **Anxiety Disorders** most commonly coded under F41.\\n\\nIf you need the official, full, or the most up-to-date descriptions (as the ICD-10-CM is updated annually), you can refer to the [CDC's ICD-10-CM code lookup tool](https://icd10cmtool.cdc.gov/) or official codebooks. Let me know if you need additional codes or details for specific disorders!\",\n    \"annotations\": null\n  },\n  \"bing_searches\": null,\n  \"annotations\": null\n}",
