              "detailedContent": "======================================================================\nFINAL READMISSION ANALYSIS\n======================================================================\n\n\ud83d\udcca READMISSION OVERVIEW:\n  Patients with readmissions: 246 / 2,652 (9.3%)\n\n\ud83e\udde0 READMISSION RISK BY DSM-5 CATEGORY:\n  Neurocognitive Disorders                       33.3% (  1/  3 patients)\n  Tic Disorders                                  21.6% ( 11/ 51 patients)\n  Other Neurodevelopmental Disorder              18.8% ( 19/101 patients)\n  Dissociative Disorders                         18.8% (  6/ 32 patients)\n  Developmental Coordination Disorder            18.2% (  2/ 11 patients)\n  Mental Disorders Due to Medical Condition      18.2% (  2/ 11 patients)\n  Psychotic Disorders                            18.2% ( 10/ 55 patients)\n  Other Mental Disorder                          17.7% ( 41/232 patients)\n  Bipolar and Related Disorders                  15.6% ( 23/147 patients)\n  Specific Learning Disorder                     15.1% ( 14/ 93 patients)\n  Personality Disorder                           14.5% ( 20/138 patients)\n  Obsessive-Compulsive and Related Disorders     14.0% ( 16/114 patients)\n  Intellectual Disability                        14.0% (  8/ 57 patients)\n  Autism Spectrum Disorder                       13.6% ( 70/513 patients)\n  Conduct Disorder                               13.6% ( 66/484 patients)\n\n\u2705 EXPORTED DATA FILES:\n  \u2713 ICD10_to_DSM5_Complete_Reference.csv - All 1,863 codes with full descriptions\n  \u2713 annotated_psychiatric_data_complete.csv - 2,652 patients with mapped diagnoses\n  \u2713 diagnoses_long_form_complete.csv - 27,884 diagnosis records with descriptions\n\n\ud83d\udccb FILES READY FOR ANALYSIS:\n  - Complete ICD-10 reference with DSM-5 TR mapping\n  - Patient-level data with diagnosis names and DSM-5 categories\n  - Long-form data for comorbidity and trend analysis\n<exited with exit code 0>",
              "content": "======================================================================\nFINAL READMISSION ANALYSIS\n======================================================================\n\n\ud83d\udcca READMISSION OVERVIEW:\n  Patients with readmissions: 246 / 2,652 (9.3%)\n\n\ud83e\udde0 READMISSION RISK BY DSM-5 CATEGORY:\n  Neurocognitive Disorders                       33.3% (  1/  3 patients)\n  Tic Disorders                                  21.6% ( 11/ 51 patients)\n  Other Neurodevelopmental Disorder              18.8% ( 19/101 patients)\n  Dissociative Disorders                         18.8% (  6/ 32 patients)\n  Developmental Coordination Disorder            18.2% (  2/ 11 patients)\n  Mental Disorders Due to Medical Condition      18.2% (  2/ 11 patients)\n  Psychotic Disorders                            18.2% ( 10/ 55 patients)\n  Other Mental Disorder                          17.7% ( 41/232 patients)\n  Bipolar and Related Disorders                  15.6% ( 23/147 patients)\n  Specific Learning Disorder                     15.1% ( 14/ 93 patients)\n  Personality Disorder                           14.5% ( 20/138 patients)\n  Obsessive-Compulsive and Related Disorders     14.0% ( 16/114 patients)\n  Intellectual Disability                        14.0% (  8/ 57 patients)\n  Autism Spectrum Disorder                       13.6% ( 70/513 patients)\n  Conduct Disorder                               13.6% ( 66/484 patients)\n\n\u2705 EXPORTED DATA FILES:\n  \u2713 ICD10_to_DSM5_Complete_Reference.csv - All 1,863 codes with full descriptions\n  \u2713 annotated_psychiatric_data_complete.csv - 2,652 patients with mapped diagnoses\n  \u2713 diagnoses_long_form_complete.csv - 27,884 diagnosis records with descriptions\n\n\ud83d\udccb FILES READY FOR ANALYSIS:\n  - Complete ICD-10 reference with DSM-5 TR mapping\n  - Patient-level data with diagnosis names and DSM-5 categories\n  - Long-form data for comorbidity and trend analysis\n<exited with exit code 0>