      "body": "Perfect! Now let me create a final summary for you:\n\n## \u2705 **ICD-10 to DSM-5 TR Mapping: COMPLETE**\n\nYour psychiatric rehospitalization data analysis is now **fully prepared** for trends and associations research. Here's what was accomplished:\n\n---\n\n### \ud83d\udcca **What You Now Have**\n\n**Three analysis-ready datasets:**\n\n1. **ICD10_to_DSM5_Complete_Reference.csv** \u2014 Master reference (1,863 codes)\n   - Every ICD-10 code with clinical description\n   - DSM-5 TR mapping for psychiatric diagnoses\n   - Frequency distribution\n\n2. **annotated_psychiatric_data_complete.csv** \u2014 Patient-level (2,652 patients)\n   - Original data plus diagnosis names for all three columns\n   - DSM-5 categories mapped for each diagnosis type\n   - Ready for regression/classification models\n\n3. **diagnoses_long_form_complete.csv** \u2014 Granular records (27,884 diagnoses)\n   - One row per diagnosis per patient\n   - Full descriptions + DSM-5 categories\n   - Ready for comorbidity networks and clustering\n\n---\n\n### \ud83c\udfaf **Key Metrics**\n\n| Metric | Value |\n|--------|-------|\n| **ICD codes mapped** | 1,863/1,863 (100%) |\n| **DSM-5 TR categories** | 31 unique categories |\n| **Psychiatric codes** | 205 with DSM-5 mapping |\n| **Diagnosis records** | 27,884 fully annotated |\n| **Coverage** | 100% \u2014 no missing descriptions |\n| **Readmission rate** | 9.3% (246/2,652 patients) |\n\n---\n\n### \ud83d\udd25 **Highest Risk Groups** (by readmission %)\n\n1. Neurocognitive Disorders \u2014 **33.3%** readmitted\n2. Tic Disorders \u2014 **21.6%**\n3. Other Neurodevelopmental \u2014 **18.8%**\n4. Dissociative Disorders \u2014 **18.8%**\n5. Autism Spectrum Disorder \u2014 **13.6%**\n\n---\n\n### \ud83d\udcdd **Files Created**\n\n- `ICD10_to_DSM5_Complete_Reference.csv` \u2014 Master lookup table\n- `annotated_psychiatric_data_complete.csv` \u2014 Patient-level analysis\n- `diagnoses_long_form_complete.csv` \u2014 Record-level analysis\n- `ANALYSIS_COMPLETE_SUMMARY.md` \u2014 Detailed documentation\n- `README_ICD_MAPPING.md` \u2014 Quick reference guide\n\n---\n\n### \ud83d\ude80 **You're Ready To:**\n\n\u2705 Perform statistical analysis (logistic regression, random forest)  \n\u2705 Identify readmission predictors  \n\u2705 Analyze comorbidity patterns  \n\u2705 Create clinical phenotypes/patient clusters  \n\u2705 Examine DSM-5 category associations with outcomes  \n\nAll ICD codes now have **real clinical descriptions** \u2014 no more placeholders!",
      "raw_time": false,
      "sender": "jupyter-ai-personas::jupyter_ai_acp_client::CopilotAcpPersona",
      "type": "msg",
      "mentions": []
