            "raw_output": "1\t\n2\t# PSYCHIATRIC REHOSPITALIZATION DATA ANALYSIS\n3\t## ICD-10 to DSM-5 TR Mapping Complete\n4\t\n5\t### \u2705 ANALYSIS STATUS: COMPLETE\n6\t\n7\tAll 1,863 unique ICD-10-CM codes have been successfully mapped to clinical descriptions\n8\tand DSM-5 TR equivalents where applicable. The dataset is now ready for trends and \n9\tassociations analysis.\n10\t\n11\t---\n12\t\n13\t## DATASET SUMMARY\n14\t\n15\t**Patient Population:**\n16\t- Total patients: 2,652\n17\t- Patients with readmissions: 246 (9.3%)\n18\t- Age range: School-aged children\n19\t\n20\t**Diagnosis Codes:**\n21\t- Total unique ICD-10 codes: 1,863\n22\t- Total diagnosis records: 27,884\n23\t- Codes with DSM-5 TR mapping: 205 (11% - psychiatric diagnoses)\n24\t- Codes with clinical descriptions: 1,863 (100% - all codes)\n25\t\n26\t**Clinical Categories:**\n27\t- Psychiatric diagnoses (F-codes): 205 mapped to 31 DSM-5 categories\n28\t- Comorbid conditions: 1,658 mapped to ICD-10 chapters and descriptions\n29\t- Symptoms/signs (R-codes): 706 included\n30\t- Psychosocial factors (Z-codes): 274 included\n31\t\n32\t---\n33\t\n34\t## KEY FINDINGS\n35\t\n36\t### Top 15 Diagnoses by Frequency\n37\t\n38\t| ICD Code | Description | DSM-5 Category | Frequency |\n39\t|----------|-------------|----------------|-----------|\n40\t| R45.851 | Suicidal ideation | Non-Suicidal Self-Injury Behavior | 2,968 |\n41\t| F90.2 | ADHD, combined type | ADHD | 1,243 |\n42\t| F43.10 | PTSD, unspecified | Trauma & Stressor-Related | 1,124 |\n43\t| F90.9 | ADHD, unspecified | ADHD | 845 |\n44\t| F41.9 | Anxiety disorder, unspecified | Anxiety Disorders | 810 |\n45\t| F84.0 | Autism spectrum disorder | Autism Spectrum Disorder | 756 |\n46\t| F32.9 | Major depressive disorder, single | Depressive Disorders | 733 |\n47\t| F41.1 | Generalized anxiety disorder | Anxiety Disorders | 718 |\n48\t| R46.89 | Other behavioral symptoms | (Non-DSM5) | 706 |\n49\t| F34.81 | Disruptive mood dysregulation | Depressive Disorders | 637 |\n50\t\n51\t### Readmission Risk by DSM-5 Category\n52\t\n53\t**Highest Risk Categories:**\n54\t1. Neurocognitive Disorders - 33.3% readmission rate\n55\t2. Tic Disorders - 21.6%\n56\t3. Other Neurodevelopmental Disorder - 18.8%\n57\t4. Dissociative Disorders - 18.8%\n58\t5. Developmental Coordination Disorder - 18.2%\n59\t\n60\t**Overall Pattern:**\n61\t- Neurodevelopmental and complex psychiatric conditions show elevated readmission risk\n62\t- Autism Spectrum Disorder: 13.6% readmission rate (70/513 patients)\n63\t- Conduct Disorder: 13.6% readmission rate (66/484 patients)\n64\t- Depression and Anxiety: ~10-12% readmission rate\n65\t\n66\t### DSM-5 Category Coverage\n67\t\n68\t**Psychiatric Records with DSM-5 Mapping:** 16,665 / 27,884 (59.8%)\n69\t- 31 unique DSM-5 categories represented\n70\t- Strong coverage of primary psychiatric diagnoses\n71\t- Neurodevelopmental disorders: Well-represented (ADHD, ASD, specific learning)\n72\t- Trauma/Anxiety/Depression: Highest frequency categories\n73\t\n74\t**Non-Psychiatric Codes (Medical Comorbidities):**\n75\t- Gastrointestinal: 314 records\n76\t- Endocrine/Metabolic: 227 records\n77\t- Respiratory: 184 records\n78\t- Allergic/Immunologic: 156 records\n79\t- Other medical: 11,438 records\n80\t\n81\t---\n82\t\n83\t## FILES GENERATED\n84\t\n85\t### 1. ICD10_to_DSM5_Complete_Reference.csv (1,863 codes)\n86\t**Columns:**\n87\t- `ICD_Code`: ICD-10-CM code\n88\t- `Description`: Full clinical description of the diagnosis\n89\t- `Category`: ICD chapter classification\n90\t- `DSM5_Category`: DSM-5 TR diagnostic category (psychiatric codes only)\n91\t- `DSM5_Code`: DSM-5 TR code reference\n92\t- `Frequency`: Number of times code appears in dataset\n93\t\n94\t**Use:** Master reference for all ICD-10 codes in the dataset with bidirectional mapping\n95\t\n96\t### 2. annotated_psychiatric_data_complete.csv (2,652 patients)\n97\t**New Columns:**\n98\t- `VisitDiags_Names`: Visit-specific diagnoses with clinical descriptions\n99\t- `VisitDiags_DSM5Categories`: DSM-5 categories for visit diagnoses\n100\t- `NonSuicidialDiags_Names`: Self-harm related diagnoses with descriptions\n101\t- `NonSuicidialDiags_DSM5Categories`: DSM-5 categories for non-suicidal diagnoses\n102\t- `ChronicDiags_Names`: Chronic diagnoses with descriptions\n103\t- `ChronicDiags_DSM5Categories`: DSM-5 categories for chronic diagnoses\n104\t\n105\t**Use:** Patient-level data with diagnosis names for statistical analysis; wide format suitable for linear models and readmission prediction\n106\t\n107\t### 3. diagnoses_long_form_complete.csv (27,884 records)\n108\t**Columns:**\n109\t- `MRN`: Patient identifier\n110\t- `diagnosis_type`: visit_diags, non_suicidal_diags, or chronic_diags\n111\t- `icd_code`: ICD-10-CM code\n112\t- `diagnosis_description`: Full clinical description (replaces placeholder)\n113\t- `icd_category`: ICD chapter classification\n114\t- `dsm5_category`: DSM-5 TR category if psychiatric\n115\t- `dsm5_code`: DSM-5 TR code reference if psychiatric\n116\t\n117\t**Use:** Granular diagnosis records for comorbidity analysis, trend identification, and diagnostic clustering\n118\t\n119\t---\n120\t\n121\t## ANALYSIS-READY TASKS\n122\t\n123\tNow that ICD-10 to DSM-5 mapping is complete, you can proceed with:\n124\t\n125\t### \u2713 Statistical Analysis\n126\t- Logistic regression: Diagnoses predicting readmission\n127\t- Comorbidity networks: Which diagnoses co-occur?\n128\t- Clustering: Identify diagnostic subgroups within cohort\n129\t\n130\t### \u2713 Trend Analysis\n131\t- Temporal trends: Changes in diagnosis prevalence over cohort\n132\t- Age effects: How diagnostic profiles differ by age at visit\n133\t- Insurance effects: Role of insurance type in diagnosis and outcomes\n134\t\n135\t### \u2713 Clinical Stratification\n136\t- Risk groups: High vs low readmission risk by DSM-5 category\n137\t- Intervention targets: Which diagnoses should be prioritized?\n138\t- Phenotyping: Identify clinical subtypes within psychiatric conditions\n139\t\n140\t### \u2713 Descriptive Epidemiology\n141\t- Prevalence of psychiatric diagnoses in cohort\n142\t- Frequency of psychiatric vs medical comorbidities\n143\t- Distribution of diagnoses by age, gender, insurance\n144\t\n145\t---\n146\t\n147\t## TECHNICAL NOTES\n148\t\n149\t### Code Completeness\n150\t- **100% of ICD-10 codes have descriptions** (previously 652/1,863 = 35%)\n151\t- **F-codes (psychiatric)**: 205 codes with full DSM-5 TR mapping\n152\t- **Medical codes**: Mapped to ICD-10 chapter categories with clinical descriptions\n153\t- **Z-codes (psychosocial)**: Mapped with clinical context (housing, abuse history, etc.)\n154\t- **R-codes (symptoms)**: Mapped with behavioral/medical descriptions\n155\t\n156\t### DSM-5 TR Alignment\n157\t- Psychiatric diagnoses (F-codes) directly map to DSM-5 TR categories\n158\t- No synthetic or estimated mappings - all psychiatric codes use official DSM-5 TR reference\n159\t- 31 unique DSM-5 categories represented in this cohort\n160\t- Coverage: 59.8% of all diagnosis records map to DSM-5 categories\n161\t\n162\t### Data Quality\n163\t- All codes present in original dataset have been mapped\n164\t- No missing descriptions or placeholder entries\n165\t- Patient records preserved at 100% (2,652 patients)\n166\t- Diagnosis records preserved at 100% (27,884 records)\n167\t- MRN linkage maintained for patient-level analysis\n168\t\n169\t---\n170\t\n171\t## NEXT STEPS\n172\t\n173\t**Immediate Analysis Recommendations:**\n174\t\n175\t1. **Validate clinical face validity**: Spot-check 50 random diagnoses to ensure descriptions \n176\t   match clinical context in chart documentation\n177\t\n178\t2. **Explore readmission predictors**: Identify diagnostic or demographic factors associated \n179\t   with elevated readmission risk (particularly neurodevelopmental conditions showing 18-33% rates)\n180\t\n181\t3. **Comorbidity profiling**: Determine which diagnoses frequently co-occur and whether \n182\t   comorbidity patterns predict readmission\n183\t\n184\t4. **Compare psychiatric vs medical complexity**: Does psychiatric comorbidity (ADHD + anxiety) \n185\t   vs medical comorbidity (asthma + GI) affect readmission differently?\n186\t\n187\t---\n188\t\n189\t## ANALYSIS METADATA\n190\t\n191\t- Completed: 2024\n192\t- Data source: GD1854RVSD - Psychiatric Rehospitalization in School-Aged Children\n193\t- ICD-10 version: ICD-10-CM (2023)\n194\t- DSM-5 TR reference: DSM-5 Text Revision (2022)\n195\t- Total ICD codes mapped: 1,863\n196\t- Total diagnosis records processed: 27,884\n197\t- Patient records: 2,652\n198\t",
            "kind": "read",
