      "body": "The notebook is open and running in JupyterLab. The first few cells (imports, feature engineering, descriptive stats, figures) will complete quickly. The ML cross-validation section (~10-fold CV for 3 models) will take a few minutes \u2014 you can watch progress in the notebook directly.\n\nHere's what the notebook produces, in order:\n\n| # | Content |\n|---|---------|\n| **Table 1** | Descriptive stats (readmitted vs not) \u2192 CSV |\n| **Fig 1** | Age histogram + readmission rate by age |\n| **Fig 2** | Demographics panel (sex, insurance, C-SSRS, restraints) |\n| **Fig 3** | Readmission rate by DSM-5 category (horizontal dot plot w/ CIs) |\n| **Fig 4** | Diagnostic complexity \u2014 violin + quartile bar chart |\n| **Fig 5** | ACE score boxplot + C-SSRS flag prevalence |\n| **Fig 6** | DSM-5 diagnosis prevalence: readmitted vs not (grouped bar) |\n| **Fig 7** | Forest plot \u2014 logistic regression odds ratios w/ interaction terms |\n| **Fig 8** | ROC curves: LR vs Random Forest vs XGBoost |\n| **Fig 9** | SHAP summary plot (XGBoost, top 20 features) |\n| **Fig 10** | Feature importance comparison: RF vs XGB |\n| **Fig 11** | SHAP dependence plots for top 3 predictors |\n\nAll figures save to `./figures/` at 300 DPI \u2014 poster-ready. Once everything finishes, let me know what you see and we can refine any figure or fix any errors that come up.",
