      "metadata": {
        "tool_calls": [
          {
            "kind": "other",
            "raw_output": "(mcp__Jupyter_MCP_Server__add_cell completed with no output)",
            "title": "mcp__Jupyter_MCP_Server__add_cell",
            "status": "completed",
            "raw_input": {
              "cell_id": "df20b1a5-d643-4166-a9ce-aeacc490fb8f",
              "cell_type": "code",
              "file_path": "Readmission_Full_Analysis.ipynb",
              "content": "\n# \u2500\u2500 Fig 14: % of charts flagged + Sensitivity/PPV at key thresholds \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nkey_thresholds = [0.05, 0.10, 0.15, 0.20, 0.25, 0.30, 0.40, 0.50]\nn_total   = len(y_ml)\nn_pos     = y_ml.sum()\nflag_pcts, sensitivities, ppvs, n_flagged_list = [], [], [], []\n\nfor thresh in key_thresholds:\n    preds = (cat_probs >= thresh).astype(int)\n    n_flag = preds.sum()\n    tn, fp, fn, tp = confusion_matrix(y_ml, preds).ravel()\n    flag_pcts.append(100 * n_flag / n_total)\n    n_flagged_list.append(n_flag)\n    sensitivities.append(100 * tp / (tp + fn) if (tp + fn) > 0 else 0)\n    ppvs.append(100 * tp / (tp + fp) if (tp + fp) > 0 else 0)\n\nxlabels = [f'{int(t*100)}%' for t in key_thresholds]\nx_pos   = np.arange(len(key_thresholds))\n\nfig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(16, 7))\n\n# Left: % of charts flagged (bars)\nbars = axes[0].bar(x_pos, flag_pcts, color=ORANGE, alpha=0.85, edgecolor='white')\naxes[0].axhline(100 * n_pos / n_total, color='black', linestyle='--', linewidth=1.5,\n                label=f'Actual readmission rate ({100*n_pos/n_total:.1f}%)')\naxes[0].set_xticks(x_pos)\naxes[0].set_xticklabels(xlabels)\nfor bar, pct, n in zip(bars, flag_pcts, n_flagged_list):\n    axes[0].text(bar.get_x() + bar.get_width()/2, pct + 0.5,\n                f'{pct:.1f}%\\n(n={n})', ha='center', fontsize=9, fontweight='bold')\naxes[0].set_xlabel('Probability Threshold')\naxes[0].set_ylabel('% of All Hospital Charts Flagged')\naxes[0].set_title('% of Charts Triggering a Flag\\nby Probability Threshold', fontsize=14, fontweight='bold')\naxes[0].legend(fontsize=11)\naxes[0].spines['top'].set_visible(False)\naxes[0].spines['right'].set_visible(False)\n\n# Right: Sensitivity and PPV\naxes[1].plot(x_pos, sensitivities, 'o-', color=BLUE, linewidth=2.5, markersize=8,\n             label='Sensitivity (% readmissions caught)')\naxes[1].plot(x_pos, ppvs, 's--', color=ORANGE, linewidth=2.5, markersize=8,\n             label='PPV (% flagged who are truly readmitted)')\nfor i, (s, p) in enumerate(zip(sensitivities, ppvs)):\n    axes[1].text(i, s + 2.5, f'{s:.0f}%', ha='center', fontsize=9, color=BLUE, fontweight='bold')\n    axes[1].text(i, p - 4,   f'{p:.0f}%', ha='center', fontsize=9, color=ORANGE, fontweight='bold')\naxes[1].set_xticks(x_pos)\naxes[1].set_xticklabels(xlabels)\naxes[1].set_xlabel('Probability Threshold')\naxes[1].set_ylabel('%')\naxes[1].set_ylim(0, 115)\naxes[1].set_title('Sensitivity & PPV by Threshold\\n(Clinical Decision Support Trade-offs)', fontsize=14, fontweight='bold')\naxes[1].legend(fontsize=11, loc='upper right')\naxes[1].spines['top'].set_visible(False)\naxes[1].spines['right'].set_visible(False)\n\nplt.suptitle('Clinical Flagging Burden vs. Benefit: CatBoost Model\\n(10-Fold CV Probabilities, n=2,652 admissions)',\n             fontsize=15, fontweight='bold', y=1.02)\nplt.tight_layout()\nplt.savefig('figures/Fig14_flagging_thresholds.png')\nplt.show()\n\n# Print decision-support table\nprint(\"\\nClinical Decision Table:\")\nprint(f\"{'Threshold':>10}  {'% Flagged':>10}  {'N Flagged':>10}  {'Sensitivity':>12}  {'PPV':>8}\")\nprint(\"-\" * 58)\nfor t, pct, n, sens, ppv in zip(key_thresholds, flag_pcts, n_flagged_list, sensitivities, ppvs):\n    print(f\"  {t*100:>5.0f}%     {pct:>8.1f}%   {n:>9}     {sens:>9.1f}%   {ppv:>6.1f}%\")\nprint(\"\u2713 Fig 14 saved\")\n"
            },
            "tool_call_id": "toolu_01HVCD2vB5tSYg5cratmRBMG"
          }
        ]
      },
      "sender": "jupyter-ai-personas::jupyter_ai_acp_client::ClaudeAcpPersona"
    },
    {
      "time": 1780268844.7289321,
      "body": "All cells are in place. Here's a summary of everything that was implemented:\n\n---\n\n**Changes made:**\n\n**CatBoost replacing XGBoost (Cells 0, 12\u201317):**\n- `auto_class_weights='Balanced'` handles the 9% readmission imbalance natively\n- `depth=4` (conservative, same as before) with `iterations=500`\n- SHAP via `TreeExplainer` works identically \u2014 values map back through the same feature/label structure\n- `cat_full.get_feature_importance()` replaces `feature_importances_` for the Fig 10 comparison\n\n**FAMD + UMAP (new Cells 18\u201319, Figs 12):**\n- Packages installed: `catboost`, `prince`, `umap-learn`\n- Binary 0/1 features are converted to string so `prince.FAMD` treats them as qualitative (CA component); continuous features (age, ACE, LOS, DSM-5 count) go through the PCA component\n- UMAP runs on the 10 FAMD components with two panels: one by readmission label (binary), one by continuous CatBoost probability (colormap)\n\n**FP vs FN graph (new Cell 20, Fig 13):**\n- Sweeps 300 thresholds from 0.01\u20130.99\n- Shows the crossover point (where FP = FN) with a purple reference line\n- Vertical dashed lines at 10/20/30/50% thresholds for clinical reference\n\n**% charts flagged (new Cell 21, Fig 14):**\n- Left panel: bar chart of flagging burden at 8 key thresholds (5\u201350%), with actual readmission rate as a dashed baseline\n- Right panel: Sensitivity and PPV at each threshold, annotated \u2014 directly shows the clinical trade-off\n- Also prints a decision-support table to the cell output",
      "raw_time": false,
      "type": "msg",
