    {
      "body": "@Gemini I need to implement one hot max in catboost for categories with 10 or less values. I'm doing this because catboost evaluated as worse than random forest and log regression in AUC-ROC. I also need you to check the FAMD setup and UMAP visualization so it visually highlights pockets of admission risk (the axes need to be named descriptively). Furthermore, catboost needs a stratified split. The evaluation of models should include cross-validation, e.g. 5-fold stratified k-fold. The clinical burden vs benefit graph needs to cover the probability threshold up to the point where false positives meet false negatives. I also need there to be a false positives vs negatives chart for random forest and log regression, and a clinical burden vs benefit graph for those models as well. Finally, there are many graphs that need confidence intervals/statistical tests/probability indicators. The readmission rate by age at admission graph needs the vertical axis expanded so the whole CI for age 6 is visible (due to a low n). It also needs indicators if any of those ages had a statistically significant association with readmission = p<0.05. Other graphs needing indicators of statistical significance at p<0.05 and confidence intervals are: sex (header should just be \"gender ID at admission\", insurance (header should just be \"insurance type\"), Any C-SSRS flag, Physical restraints used, ACE score of 4 or higher vs 3 or lower, diagnostic complexity quartile.",
