    {
      "raw_time": false,
      "type": "msg",
      "body": "@Gemini That looks good. One other thing to add would be comparing the readmission rates of no C-SSRS flag vs red flag, with statistical significance and confidence intervals. Diagnostic complexity quartiles should be defined (boundaries of each quartile). The bars of each quartile should be the same color. For the readmission rate by dsm-5 diagnostic category, orange should be used for the categories w/ n geq 15 where the lower bound of the CI did not cross the overall rate (9.3%). Furthermore, the logistic regression/odds ratio calculations and graph needs work. NSSI x C-SSRS flag should be considered with the red flag, since that was the only one that appeared to be associated with readmission. Age x public insurance should be measured. In addition to \"any C-SSRS flag\", the \"level\" of flag should be measured, i.e. 0 flag (no flag), 1 flag (yellow), 2 flag (orange), 3 flag (red). I'm concerned with a few of the data points in the log regression calculation, since they don't have confidence intervals visible: length of stay and diagnostic complexity x age. Finally, the \"other mental disorder\" category in the DSM needs to be subcategorized somehow, because that's not a helpful label.\n\n\n",
      "id": "b2c93f31-fcc7-4cc7-bf73-8110ed2a29d4",
