    {
      "time": 1780280369.962801,
      "mentions": [],
      "raw_time": false,
      "sender": "jupyter-ai-personas::jupyter_ai_acp_client::GeminiAcpPersona",
      "body": "I have completed all the requested updates to the `Readmission_Full_Analysis.ipynb` notebook. Here is a summary of the changes:\n\n### **1. Modeling & Cross-Validation**\n*   **5-Fold Stratified CV**: Updated the cross-validation from 10-fold to 5-fold for all models.\n*   **CatBoost Improvements**: Implemented dynamic `cat_features_idx` detection. Features with $\\le 10$ unique values are now automatically identified, cast to integers, and passed to the model to properly utilize `one_hot_max_size=10`.\n*   **Standardized Features**: Standard-scaled continuous variables (`age`, `los_days`, `ace_score`, `n_dsm5_categories`, `complexity_x_age`) for the logistic regression. This ensures the Odds Ratios and their 95% Confidence Intervals are properly scaled and visible in the forest plot.\n\n### **2. Feature Engineering & Subcategorization**\n*   **Homicidal Ideation**: Renamed the generic \"Other Mental Disorder\" DSM-5 category to \"Homicidal Ideation\" (based on 100% representation by ICD-10 code R45.850).\n*   **C-SSRS Ordinal Level**: Replaced the binary \"Any Flag\" with an ordinal scale (0=None, 1=Yellow, 2=Orange, 3=Red).\n*   **Updated Interactions**:\n    *   Changed `nssi_x_csrss` to specifically target the **Red Flag** interaction (`nssi_x_csrss_red`).\n    *   Added a new interaction term: `age_x_public_insurance`.\n\n### **3. Enhanced Visualizations & Statistical Tests**\n*   **Descriptive UMAP Axes**: Renamed UMAP axes to `UMAP Dimension 1 (Clinical/Demographic Profile)` and `UMAP Dimension 2 (Diagnostic Complexity)`.\n*   **Dynamic Decision Metrics**: Refactored Figs 13 and 14 to loop over CatBoost, Random Forest, and Logistic Regression. The clinical burden charts now truncate at the specific threshold where False Positives cross False Negatives.\n*   **Statistical Significance (p < 0.05)**:\n    *   **Fig 1 (Age)**: Expanded the Y-axis (0-45%) to show the full CI for age 6 and added `*` markers for significant ages.\n    *   **Fig 2 (Demographics)**: Updated headers to \"Gender ID at Admission\" and \"Insurance Type\", added error bars, and included p-values in the titles.\n    *   **Fig 3 (DSM-5 Categories)**: Added CIs and implemented the requested orange coloring logic ($n \\ge 15$ and lower bound of CI $> 9.3\\%$).\n    *   **Fig 4 (Complexity)**: Added boundary labels to quartiles (e.g., \"Q1 (1-2 categories)\"), unified the bar colors, and added significance tests vs. Q1.\n    *   **Fig 5 (ACE/C-SSRS)**: Added a new comparison chart for \"No Flag vs. Red Flag\" with CIs, and a binary significance test for \"ACE $\\ge 4$ vs. $\\le 3$\".\n\nThe notebook is now fully updated and ready for execution.",
      "id": "b8a7fd03-fffb-4b22-9313-9d96884c8822",
      "type": "msg"
    },
    {
      "type": "msg",
      "body": "@Gemini  A couple things to update. Some descriptive statistics to add: Number of readmissions as a continuous variable with mean # of readmissions, SD, percent readmitted. ACEs score with median, average, SD, and N/percent collected. LOS with median, average, SD. # of Visit, chronic, and non-suicidial diags, with median, average, and SD. Medical comorbidity breakdown by major types (assuming this is chronic diags?) Add a star on physical restraints used to denote p<0.001. The star for significance on readmission rate by diagnostic complexity quartile is clipping into the graph title. Any graph with a statistically significant difference (P<0.05) needs a specific p value, not just a star. Most importantly, there's a keyerror in the logistic regression block: \"---------------------------------------------------------------------------\nKeyError                                  Traceback (most recent call last)\nFile ~/code/jupyter_projects/.venv/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pandas/core/indexes/base.py:3641, in Index.get_loc(self, key)\n   3640 try:\n-> 3641     return self._engine.get_loc(casted_key)\n   3642 except KeyError as err:\n\nFile pandas/_libs/index.pyx:168, in pandas._libs.index.IndexEngine.get_loc()\n--> 168 'Could not get source, probably due dynamically evaluated source code.'\n\nFile pandas/_libs/index.pyx:197, in pandas._libs.index.IndexEngine.get_loc()\n--> 197 'Could not get source, probably due dynamically evaluated source code.'\n\nFile pandas/_libs/hashtable_class_helper.pxi:7668, in pandas._libs.hashtable.PyObjectHashTable.get_item()\n-> 7668 'Could not get source, probably due dynamically evaluated source code.'\n\nFile pandas/_libs/hashtable_class_helper.pxi:7676, in pandas._libs.hashtable.PyObjectHashTable.get_item()\n-> 7676 'Could not get source, probably due dynamically evaluated source code.'\n\nKeyError: 'csrss_red'\n\nThe above exception was the direct cause of the following exception:\n\nKeyError                                  Traceback (most recent call last)\nCell In[24], line 11\n      9 model_df['nssi_x_csrss']   = model_df['has_nssi'] * model_df['csrss_any']\n     10 model_df['complexity_x_age'] = model_df['n_dsm5_categories'] * model_df['age']\n---> 11 model_df['csrss_level'] = (model_df['csrss_red'] * 3 + model_df['csrss_orange'] * 2 + model_df['csrss_yellow'] * 1).fillna(0).astype(int)\n     12 model_df['nssi_x_csrss_red'] = model_df['has_nssi'] * model_df['csrss_red']\n     13 model_df['age_x_public_insurance'] = model_df['age'] * model_df['insurance_public']\n\nFile ~/code/jupyter_projects/.venv/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pandas/core/frame.py:4378, in DataFrame.__getitem__(self, key)\n   4374 \n   4375         if is_single_key:\n   4376             if self.columns.nlevels > 1:\n   4377                 return self._getitem_multilevel(key)\n-> 4378             indexer = self.columns.get_loc(key)\n   4379             if is_integer(indexer):\n   4380                 indexer = [indexer]\n   4381         else:\n\nFile ~/code/jupyter_projects/.venv/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pandas/core/indexes/base.py:3648, in Index.get_loc(self, key)\n   3643     if isinstance(casted_key, slice) or (\n   3644         isinstance(casted_key, abc.Iterable)\n   3645         and any(isinstance(x, slice) for x in casted_key)\n   3646     ):\n   3647         raise InvalidIndexError(key) from err\n-> 3648     raise KeyError(key) from err\n   3649 except TypeError:\n   3650     # If we have a listlike key, _check_indexing_error will raise\n   3651     #  InvalidIndexError. Otherwise we fall through and re-raise\n   3652     #  the TypeError.\n   3653     self._check_indexing_error(key)\n\nKeyError: 'csrss_red'\"",
