      "sender": "66b5de9aa1ae4e47a45824fbb597caf1",
      "body": "@Claude the p value for quartile 4 is still clipping in diagnostic complexity graph. furthermore, unecessary indents keep getting added that throw errors in the runtime. The diagnostic category graph needs the bar colors changed, dissociative has the lower CI bar crossing the overall rate but is still orange, and ASD, conduct disorder, trauma and stressor disorders, anxiety disorders, and ADHD all do not cross the overall rate but are blue. The title for the no flag vs red flag graph is messed up; it reads \"readmission rate: no flag vs red flag\\np=0.568\". Many of the titles for the cohort overview are messed up; \"readmission counts\\n(Mean=0.1, SD=.34), ACE score distribution\\n(n=1569 [59.2% collected]), Length of stay (LOS\\n(Median=8.0, mean = 10.0). The diagnostic burdens chart is unclear, it can just be scrapped. ACE score distribution needs a mean and SD. LOS needs an SD. The catboost block is throwing an error: \"---------------------------------------------------------------------------\nCatBoostError                             Traceback (most recent call last)\nCell In[43], line 51\n     49 cat_probs = np.zeros(len(y_ml))\n     50 for train_idx, test_idx in cv.split(X_ml, y_ml):\n---> 51     cat_model.fit(X_ml[train_idx], y_ml[train_idx])\n     52     cat_probs[test_idx] = cat_model.predict_proba(X_ml[test_idx])[:, 1]\n     53     early_stopping_rounds=30\n\nFile ~/code/jupyter_projects/.venv/lib/python3.14/site-packages/catboost/core.py:5547, in CatBoostClassifier.fit(self, X, y, cat_features, text_features, embedding_features, graph, sample_weight, baseline, use_best_model, eval_set, verbose, logging_level, plot, plot_file, column_description, verbose_eval, metric_period, silent, early_stopping_rounds, save_snapshot, snapshot_file, snapshot_interval, init_model, callbacks, log_cout, log_cerr)\n   5544 if 'loss_function' in params:\n   5545     CatBoostClassifier._check_is_compatible_loss(params['loss_function'])\n-> 5547 self._fit(X, y, cat_features, text_features, embedding_features, None, graph, sample_weight, None, None, None, None, baseline, use_best_model,\n   5548           eval_set, verbose, logging_level, plot, plot_file, column_description, verbose_eval, metric_period,\n   5549           silent, early_stopping_rounds, save_snapshot, snapshot_file, snapshot_interval, init_model, callbacks, log_cout, log_cerr)\n   5550 return self\n\nFile ~/code/jupyter_projects/.venv/lib/python3.14/site-packages/catboost/core.py:2701, in CatBoost._fit(self, X, y, cat_features, text_features, embedding_features, pairs, graph, sample_weight, group_id, group_weight, subgroup_id, pairs_weight, baseline, use_best_model, eval_set, verbose, logging_level, plot, plot_file, column_description, verbose_eval, metric_period, silent, early_stopping_rounds, save_snapshot, snapshot_file, snapshot_interval, init_model, callbacks, log_cout, log_cerr)\n   2698 if y is None and not isinstance(X, PATH_TYPES + (Pool,)):\n   2699     raise CatBoostError(\"y may be None only when X is an instance of catboost.Pool or string\")\n-> 2701 train_params = self._prepare_train_params(\n   2702     X=X, y=y, cat_features=cat_features, text_features=text_features, embedding_features=embedding_features,\n   2703     pairs=pairs, graph=graph, sample_weight=sample_weight, group_id=group_id, group_weight=group_weight,\n   2704     subgroup_id=subgroup_id, pairs_weight=pairs_weight, baseline=baseline, use_best_model=use_best_model,\n   2705     eval_set=eval_set, verbose=verbose, logging_level=logging_level, plot=plot, plot_file=plot_file,\n   2706     column_description=column_description, verbose_eval=verbose_eval, metric_period=metric_period,\n   2707     silent=silent, early_stopping_rounds=early_stopping_rounds, save_snapshot=save_snapshot,\n   2708     snapshot_file=snapshot_file, snapshot_interval=snapshot_interval, init_model=init_model,\n   2709     callbacks=callbacks\n   2710 )\n   2711 params = train_params[\"params\"]\n   2712 train_pool = train_params[\"train_pool\"]\n\nFile ~/code/jupyter_projects/.venv/lib/python3.14/site-packages/catboost/core.py:2581, in CatBoost._prepare_train_params(self, X, y, cat_features, text_features, embedding_features, pairs, graph, sample_weight, group_id, group_weight, subgroup_id, pairs_weight, baseline, use_best_model, eval_set, verbose, logging_level, plot, plot_file, column_description, verbose_eval, metric_period, silent, early_stopping_rounds, save_snapshot, snapshot_file, snapshot_interval, init_model, callbacks)\n   2578 text_features = _process_feature_indices(text_features, X, params, 'text_features')\n   2579 embedding_features = _process_feature_indices(embedding_features, X, params, 'embedding_features')\n-> 2581 train_pool = _build_train_pool(X, y, cat_features, text_features, embedding_features, pairs, graph,\n   2582                                sample_weight, group_id, group_weight, subgroup_id, pairs_weight,\n   2583                                baseline, column_description)\n   2584 if train_pool.is_empty_:\n   2585     raise CatBoostError(\"X is empty.\")\n\nFile ~/code/jupyter_projects/.venv/lib/python3.14/site-packages/catboost/core.py:1540, in _build_train_pool(X, y, cat_features, text_features, embedding_features, pairs, graph, sample_weight, group_id, group_weight, subgroup_id, pairs_weight, baseline, column_description)\n   1538     if y is None:\n   1539         raise CatBoostError(\"y has not initialized in fit(): X is not catboost.Pool object, y must be not None in fit().\")\n-> 1540     train_pool = Pool(X, y, cat_features=cat_features, text_features=text_features, embedding_features=embedding_features, pairs=pairs, graph=graph, weight=sample_weight, group_id=group_id,\n   1541                       group_weight=group_weight, subgroup_id=subgroup_id, pairs_weight=pairs_weight, baseline=baseline)\n   1542 return train_pool\n\nFile ~/code/jupyter_projects/.venv/lib/python3.14/site-packages/catboost/core.py:805, in Pool.__init_