    {
      "body": "All 5 cells fixed. Here's what changed in each:\n\n**CatBoost (Cell 14):** Removed `cat_features_idx`, `cat_features=`, `one_hot_max_size`, `l2_leaf_reg`, and the dangling `early_stopping_rounds=30` line. The model now receives a clean float array with no categorical feature declaration \u2014 which is all it needs. Restored `iterations=500` and `verbose=0`.\n\n**Fig 3 colors (Cell 5):** Replaced `rate >= 20` threshold with `(rate - ci) > overall_rate` \u2014 a bar is now orange only if its **lower CI bound** strictly exceeds the overall rate (9.3%), meaning it's statistically elevated. Dissociative will correctly flip to blue; ADHD, ASD, Conduct, Trauma, Anxiety will now be orange only if their lower CI clears the line.\n\n**Fig 4 p-val clipping (Cell 6):** Added `axes[1].set_ylim(0, max_top * 1.55)` computed from actual data before any annotation, giving consistent headroom. Also cleaned up the `proportions_ztest` call to avoid double-computation and use `itertuples` to avoid the stale index issue.\n\n**No-flag vs Red-flag title (Cell 7):** Fixed `\\\\n` \u2192 `\\n` so the p-value appears on a second line. Added n-labels and rate labels to the bars, set proper ylim, and saved to `Fig5b_no_flag_vs_red_flag.png`.\n\n**Cohort overview (Cell 11):** Fixed all `\\\\n` \u2192 `\\n`. Added `Mean\u00b1SD` to the ACE title. Added `\u00b1SD` to the LOS title. **Scrapped the Diagnostic Burdens panel** \u2014 grid is now 2\u00d72 (Readmission Counts, ACE Score, LOS, Prevalence Pie).",
