      "body": "@Claude the p value for age 12 is clipping into the n, it needs to be moved up. The % and n for readmission rates by demographic and clinical characteristics need to be moved up as well, they're clipping into the CI bars. Please add SHAP feature importance for random forest, and SHAP dependence plots for the top 3 random forest predictors. Please explain what is meant by \"clinical/demographic profile\" for UMAP dimension 1; it's not clear like diagnostic complexity. I also noticed that the crossover point of fp and fn for catboost and random forest is not reflected in the burden vs benefit chart for either; both only go to the probability threshold of 0.5. catboost should go to .65 and random forest should go to .6, with the crossover probability threshold highlighted on the burden vs benefit graphs. that goes for the more descriptive burden vs benefit graph, which should have entries for log regression and random forest as well, and probability thresholds up to .65 for catboost, .6 for random forest.",
