      "mentions": [],
      "raw_time": false,
      "time": 1780286433.830677,
      "body": "All done. Here's a summary of every change:\n\n---\n\n**Fig 1 \u2014 Age 12 p-value clipping:** n labels now sit `+1` above the bar body; p-values sit `+ci+3.5` above the CI whisker. `ylim` is set dynamically to `max(rate + ci) \u00d7 1.55`, so there's always room.\n\n**Fig 2 \u2014 % and n clipping into CI bars:** Labels now positioned at `rate + err + 1.0` (above the CI cap), not at the fixed `+0.5` that was inside the whisker. `ylim` also set dynamically to `max(rate + err) \u00d7 1.55`.\n\n**SHAP for Random Forest (2 new cells after Fig 11):**\n- **Fig 9b** \u2014 SHAP beeswarm summary plot for `rf_full` (same style as CatBoost Fig 9). Uses `shap_values_rf[1]` (class-1 values) since sklearn RF returns a list per class.\n- **Fig 11b** \u2014 SHAP dependence plots for the top 3 RF features by `rf_imp`.\n\n**UMAP axis labels:** Removed `(Clinical/Demographic Profile)` and `(Diagnostic Complexity)` interpretive labels \u2014 axes are now plain `UMAP 1` / `UMAP 2`. UMAP axes are abstract embedding coordinates; they don't have inherent meaning like a named factor. The subtitle now says \"(axes are abstract embedding coordinates)\" to be explicit. If you want to interpret a dimension, the right approach would be to correlate each embedding axis with individual features \u2014 that's a separate post-hoc analysis.\n\n**Fig 13 \u2014 FP vs FN:** Now a 1\u00d73 figure showing all three models side-by-side. CatBoost sweeps to 0.65, RF to 0.60, LR to 0.50. Each panel marks its FP=FN crossover with a purple dotted line.\n\n**Fig 14 \u2014 Burden vs Benefit:** Fully redesigned as a 2\u00d73 grid (models as columns, % flagged on top row, sensitivity+PPV on bottom row). CatBoost extends to 0.65, RF to 0.60, LR to 0.50. The FP/FN crossover is highlighted as a purple dotted vertical line on both rows of each model's column."
    },
    {
      "mentions": [
        "jupyter-ai-personas::jupyter_ai_acp_client::ClaudeAcpPersona"
      ],
      "id": "bded4fec-d10b-4725-b6a9-f096cd90f449",
      "type": "msg",
      "raw_time": false,
      "body": "@Claude  Go ahead and correlate each embedding axis with individual features to identify the clusters. Any other useful post-hoc analyses I can do?",
      "time": 1780286493.844691,
      "sender": "66b5de9aa1ae4e47a45824fbb597caf1"
    },
    {
      "mentions": [],
      "raw_time": false,
      "body": "Let me add the correlation analysis cells first, then give you the full post-hoc menu.",
      "sender": "jupyter-ai-personas::jupyter_ai_acp_client::ClaudeAcpPersona",
      "type": "msg",
      "id": "523b2c2b-984b-4e08-8759-dc39509940e0",
      "time": 1780286534.807306
    },
    {
      "time": 1780286535.627126,
      "id": "bfb955de-fcb6-438e-9016-a00117672a25",
      "metadata": {
        "tool_calls": [
          {
            "title": "mcp__Jupyter_MCP_Server__add_cell",
            "raw_output": "(mcp__Jupyter_MCP_Server__add_cell completed with no output)",
            "kind": "other",
            "raw_input": {
              "content": "\n# \u2500\u2500 UMAP Axis Interpretation: Spearman correlations with all features \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nfrom scipy.stats import spearmanr\n\ncorr_records = []\nfor i, feat in enumerate(feature_labels):\n    r1, p1 = spearmanr(embedding[:, 0], X_ml[:, i])\n    r2, p2 = spearmanr(embedding[:, 1], X_ml[:, i])\n    corr_records.append({'feature': feat, 'r_umap1': r1, 'p_umap1': p1,\n                         'r_umap2': r2, 'p_umap2': p2})\n\ncorr_df = pd.DataFrame(corr_records)\ntop_u1  = corr_df.reindex(corr_df['r_umap1'].abs().sort_values(ascending=False).index).head(12)\ntop_u2  = corr_df.reindex(corr_df['r_umap2'].abs().sort_values(ascending=False).index).head(12)\n\nprint(\"\u2500\u2500 Top correlates with UMAP 1 \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\")\nfor _, row in top_u1.iterrows():\n    sig = '***' if row['p_umap1'] < 0.001 else ('**' if row['p_umap1'] < 0.01 else '*' if row['p_umap1'] < 0.05 else '')\n    print(f\"  {row['feature']:<35}  r = {row['r_umap1']:+.3f}  {sig}\")\n\nprint(\"\\n\u2500\u2500 Top correlates with UMAP 2 \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\")\nfor _, row in top_u2.iterrows():\n    sig = '***' if row['p_umap2'] < 0.001 else ('**' if row['p_umap2'] < 0.01 else '*' if row['p_umap2'] < 0.05 else '')\n    print(f\"  {row['feature']:<35}  r = {row['r_umap2']:+.3f}  {sig}\")\n\n# \u2500\u2500 Ranked bar charts \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nfig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(16, 7))\n\nfor ax, top_df, rcol, pcol, title in [\n    (axes[0], top_u1, 'r_umap1', 'p_umap1', 'UMAP 1 \u2014 Feature Correlations (Spearman r)'),\n    (axes[1], top_u2, 'r_umap2', 'p_umap2', 'UMAP 2 \u2014 Feature Correlations (Spearman r)'),\n]:\n    top_df = top_df.sort_values(rcol)\n    colors = [ORANGE if r > 0 else BLUE for r in top_df[rcol]]\n    bars = ax.barh(top_df['feature'], top_df[rcol], color=colors, alpha=0.85, edgecolor='white')\n    ax.axvline(0, color='black', linewidth=0.8)\n    # Star annotations\n    for bar, (_, row) in zip(bars, top_df.iterrows()):\n        p = row[pcol]\n        sig = '***' if p < 0.001 else ('**' if p < 0.01 else '*' if p < 0.05 else '')\n        x = row[rcol]\n        ax.text(x + (0.005 if x >= 0 else -0.005), bar.get_y() + bar.get_height()/2,\n                sig, va='center', ha='left' if x >= 0 else 'right', fontsize=10, color='black')\n    ax.set_xlabel('Spearman r')\n    ax.set_title(title, fontsize=13, fontweight='bold')\n    ax.spines['top'].set_visible(False)\n    ax.spines['right'].set_visible(False)\n\nplt.suptitle('Which Features Drive Each UMAP Dimension?\\n'\n             '(Orange = positive correlation; Blue = negative)',\n             fontsize=14, fontweight='bold', y=1.02)\nplt.tight_layout()\nplt.savefig('figures/Fig12b_UMAP_feature_correlations.png')\nplt.show()\nprint(\"\u2713 Fig 12b saved\")\n",
              "cell_id": "4e876b0c-1396-4bc7-85aa-fb099a375a57",
              "file_path": "Readmission_Full_Analysis.ipynb",
              "cell_type": "code"
            },
            "tool_call_id": "toolu_012tZAtyvzPrrDQ1VcFNeAYN",
