      "body": "@Claude please implement all of these, in addition to binary comparisons of statistical significance for dsm diagnostic category presence in the prevalence graph, a SHAP feature importance by impact on readmission probability chart like the one for catboost, fix block 102, the SHAP plot for random forest, and display a max and min for length of stay. I'd also like to denote significant protective factors against readmission but the only one I remember seeing is age 12, is that right? Additionally, there was an error in the SHAP dependence plots block: \"ValueError                                Traceback (most recent call last)\nCell In[100], line 8\n      6 for ax, feat_label in zip(axes, rf_imp_top3):\n      7     feat_idx = feature_labels.index(feat_label)\n----> 8     shap.dependence_plot(\n      9         feat_idx, shap_rf_pos, X_ml,\n     10         feature_names=feature_labels,\n     11         ax=ax, show=False, dot_size=12, alpha=0.4\n     12     )\n     13     ax.set_title(f'SHAP Dependence: {feat_label}', fontsize=13, fontweight='bold')\n     14     ax.spines['top'].set_visible(False)\n\nFile ~/code/jupyter_projects/.venv/lib/python3.14/site-packages/shap/plots/_scatter.py:634, in dependence_legacy(ind, shap_values, features, feature_names, display_features, interaction_index, color, axis_color, cmap, dot_size, x_jitter, alpha, title, xmin, xmax, ax, show, ymin, ymax)\n    632 if not hasattr(ind, \"__len__\"):\n    633     if interaction_index == \"auto\":\n--> 634         interaction_index = approximate_interactions(ind, shap_values, features)[0]\n    635     interaction_index = convert_name(interaction_index, shap_values, feature_names)\n    636 categorical_interaction = False\n\nFile ~/code/jupyter_projects/.venv/lib/python3.14/site-packages/shap/utils/_general.py:161, in approximate_interactions(index, shap_values, X, feature_names)\n    159     for j in range(0, len(x), inc):\n    160         if np.std(val_other[j : j + inc]) > 0 and n