      "mentions": [],
      "body": "All 7 new analysis cells are added. Here's a complete summary of everything done this session:\n\n---\n\n**Fixes:**\n\n| Cell | Fix |\n|------|-----|\n| RF SHAP summary (block ~102) | Handles all 3 SHAP output formats (list, 3D array, 2D array) for sklearn RF version compatibility |\n| RF SHAP dependence | Added `interaction_index=None` \u2014 disables the `approximate_interactions` auto-detection that was calling `np.corrcoef` on mismatched shapes |\n| CatBoost SHAP dependence | Same `interaction_index=None` fix proactively |\n| Fig 6 DSM prevalence | Chi-squared with Bonferroni correction; red markers = risk factor, teal = protective |\n| Cohort viz LOS title | Now shows Min / Median / Mean\u00b1SD / Max |\n| Fig 1 age distribution | Significantly **elevated** ages shown in red, significantly **protective** ages shown in teal; prints a summary table of which ages qualify |\n\n**On the protective factor question:** Age 12 may indeed show as protective \u2014 you'll see the answer in the Fig 1 cell output when it runs (it prints the exact p-values and which ages pass). Worth noting that `age` as a continuous predictor in the logistic regression was not significant (p=0.21), so age 12 specifically being protective is a per-stratum finding, not a regression effect.\n\n**New analysis cells:**\n\n1. **FAMD Loadings Heatmap** \u2014 Shows Pearson r between each feature and each FAMD component; directly answers which features drive the UMAP structure\n2. **HDBSCAN Cluster Profiling** \u2014 Finds natural patient clusters in UMAP space; produces a clinical profile table (readmission rate, demographics, diagnoses per cluster) saved to CSV\n3. **Decision Curve Analysis** \u2014 Net benefit curves for all 3 models vs. treat-all / treat-none; shows the threshold range where screening is actually beneficial\n4. **Calibration Curves** \u2014 Reliability diagrams plus probability distribution histograms; tells you whether p=0.20 from the model actually means 20% real-world risk\n5. **DeLong Test (bootstrap)** \u2014 Pairwise AUC comparisons with 95% CI and p-values for all 3 model pairs\n6. **Subgroup AUC** \u2014 Per-model AUC for 12 subgroups (age, sex, insurance, ACE, trauma, restraints); dot plot + CSV export; the key equity analysis\n7. **SHAP Interaction Values** \u2014 Top 15\u00d715 interaction heatmap for CatBoost; printed ranking of top 10 interacting feature pairs",
