      "body": "Good \u2014 36 cells total. The CatBoost SHAP interactions cell is at `3513faba` (index 34). Now making all three fixes in parallel, then adding the RF SHAP interactions cell.\n\n**On the -1/-2 issue:** `shap.dependence_plot` adds x-jitter to integer/binary features, which can push 0-valued points to negative x. The fix is a manual scatter plot using the raw `X_ml` values \u2014 no jitter, no library surprises. The negative SHAP *y*-values are expected (they mean the feature is reducing predicted readmission risk).",
