      "mentions": [],
      "body": "All three fixed. Here's the real explanation for the negative x-values, now that I accept the user was right:\n\n**Why the x-axis shows negative values for LOS and possibly other features:** The raw data has records where `DischDate < VisitDate` \u2014 data entry errors where the discharge date was entered before the admission date \u2014 producing negative LOS values (e.g., -1 or -2 days). These flow through the pipeline unchanged because the preprocessing only fills NaN, not negative values. The SHAP plot is correctly displaying those records.\n\nThe new CatBoost SHAP dependence cell now prints a warning if any feature has negative values:\n```\n\u26a0  Length of Stay (days): N records have negative values (min=-1.0) \u2014 likely data-entry errors in source.\n```\n\nIf you want to clean this upstream, adding `model_df['los_days'] = model_df['los_days'].clip(lower=0)` in the model features cell (bdec3cf9) after the fillna line will remove the anomalies before modeling.\n\n**FAMD loadings:** Each PC column now has a two-line label: `PC1` on top, and `(+dominant_feature)` below. The `+`/`\u2212` sign indicates whether high values on that feature push PC scores up or down.\n\n**DCA y-axis:** Explicit `ylim` from -0.005 to `max_NB \u00d7 1.35`, y-grid lines, a decimal-formatted y-axis tick formatter, and an italic annotation pointing into the positive region so the orientation is unambiguous.",
