    {
      "body": "This `ImportError` happens because of a version incompatibility between the `statsmodels` and `scipy` packages installed in your virtual environment.\n\nSpecifically:\n- You currently have `scipy==1.17.1` and `statsmodels==0.14.4` installed. \n- Recent versions of SciPy (1.16+) removed an internal function (`_lazywhere`) that `statsmodels` 0.14.4 was trying to use. \n- The `statsmodels` team has since fixed this compatibility issue in version `0.14.5` and newer.\n\n**Proposed Strategy:**\nTo fix this, we should upgrade `statsmodels` to the latest version (`0.14.6`) by running:\n`.venv/bin/pip install --upgrade statsmodels`\n\nDoes this strategy sound good to you? If so, I will draft a quick plan to execute this command and update your environment.",
