    {
      "body": "**Diagnostic complexity** is the **count of unique DSM\u20115 categories** for each patient, derived from the semicolon\u2011separated `VisitDiags_DSM5Categories` and `ChronicDiags_DSM5Categories` fields. The interaction is computed as:\n\n```\ncomplexity_x_age = age * n_dsm5_categories\n```\n\nSo with age 5\u201312 and, say, 0\u20138 categories, the x\u2011axis naturally spans 0\u201396 (\u22480\u2013100). It\u2019s not a scaled value\u2014just age multiplied by the category count.",
      "mentions": [],
      "id": "d562be75-b3c0-4b8d-a515-b0f7c351ec4d",
      "raw_time": false,
      "time": 1780308638.0050461,
