    {
      "mentions": [],
      "body": "Updated the DCA cell to set y\u2011limits from the full min/max net\u2011benefit range with padding (so **Screen All** is visible) and moved the positive\u2011NB caption to the top\u2011left with a white background so it no longer clips. Re\u2011run the DCA cell to regenerate the figure.\n\nOn foundation models: for a tabular clinical dataset of this size, a large FM is **more likely to overfit** than to outperform CatBoost/RF unless you have substantially more data and careful regularization/external validation. In practice, boosted trees are still the strongest baseline for tabular data; an FM is not automatically the \u201cnext step up.\u201d",
      "raw_time": false,
      "id": "69fd7ade-d0ac-488d-9324-b33fcd4db915",
