      "time": 1780310796.84147,
      "mentions": [],
      "body": "Yes \u2014 but only **post\u2011hoc**, based on the cluster\u2019s dominant features. HDBSCAN doesn\u2019t produce semantic labels; we derive them by profiling each cluster (e.g., top z\u2011score deviations in diagnoses, LOS, ACE, demographics) and then assign human\u2011readable names like \u201cHigh\u2011complexity/High\u2011ACE\u201d or \u201cYounger/Neurodev\u2011heavy.\u201d I can add those labels directly to the cluster summary table and annotate the UMAP plot.",
      "id": "55e62b82-d158-4bf9-8628-f2b293ca21a1",
      "raw_time": false
    },
