                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "### Cell 13\n\n#### Metadata\n\n```yaml\nexecution_count: 13\ntype: code\n```\n\n#### Source\n\n```python\n\n# \u2500\u2500 Logistic regression model + interaction terms \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nimport statsmodels.api as sm\n\n# Add clinically motivated interaction terms\nmodel_df['age_x_conduct']  = model_df['age'] * model_df['has_conduct']\nmodel_df['age_x_asd']      = model_df['age'] * model_df['has_asd']\nmodel_df['ace_x_trauma']   = model_df['ace_score'] * model_df['has_trauma']\nmodel_df['nssi_x_csrss']   = model_df['has_nssi'] * model_df['csrss_any']\nmodel_df['complexity_x_age'] = model_df['n_dsm5_categories'] * model_df['age']\nmodel_df['csrss_level'] = (model_df['csrss_red'] * 3 + model_df['csrss_orange'] * 2 + model_df['csrss_yellow'] * 1).fillna(0).astype(int)\nmodel_df['nssi_x_csrss_red'] = model_df['has_nssi'] * model_df['csrss_red']\nmodel_df['age_x_public_insurance'] = model_df['age'] * model_df['insurance_public']\n\n# Preserve unscaled values for SHAP dependence x-axes\nmodel_df_unscaled = model_df.copy()\n\n# Standardize continuous variables for Odds Ratio interpretation and visible CIs\nfrom sklearn.preprocessing import StandardScaler\nscaler = StandardScaler()\nscale_cols = ['age', 'los_days', 'ace_score', 'n_dsm5_categories', 'complexity_x_age']\nmodel_df[scale_cols] = scaler.fit_transform(model_df[scale_cols])\n\ninteraction_labels = {\n    'age_x_conduct':    'Age \u00d7 Conduct Disorder',\n    'age_x_asd':        'Age \u00d7 ASD',\n    'ace_x_trauma':     'ACE Score \u00d7 Trauma/PTSD',\n    'nssi_x_csrss_red': 'NSSI \u00d7 C-SSRS Red Flag',\n    'complexity_x_age': 'Diagnostic Complexity \u00d7 Age',\n    'age_x_public_insurance': 'Age \u00d7 Public Insurance',\n}\n\nall_x_cols = [c for c in feat_cols if c != 'csrss_any'] + list(interaction_labels.keys()) + ['csrss_level']\nX = sm.add_constant(model_df[all_x_cols])\ny = model_df['readmitted']\n\nlogit_model = sm.Logit(y, X).fit(maxiter=200)\nprint(logit_model.summary2())\n```\n\n#### Output\n\n```\nOptimization terminated successfully.\n         Current function value: 0.285844\n         Iterations 7\n                            Results: Logit\n=======================================================================\nModel:                Logit              Method:             MLE       \nDependent Variable:   readmitted         Pseudo R-squared:   0.075     \nDate:                 2026-06-01 03:06   AIC:                1566.1155 \nNo. Observations:     2652               BIC:                1713.1923 \nDf Model:             24                 Log-Likelihood:     -758.06   \nDf Residuals:         2627               LL-Null:            -819.14   \nConverged:            1.0000             LLR p-value:        3.9743e-15\nNo. Iterations:       7.0000             Scale:              1.0000    \n-----------------------------------------------------------------------\n                         Coef.  Std.Err.    z    P>|z|   [0.025  0.975]\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------\nconst                   -3.7621   0.3983 -9.4442 0.0000 -4.5428 -2.9813\nage                     -0.0729   0.2352 -0.3098 0.7567 -0.5338  0.3881\ngender_male             -0.0437   0.1558 -0.2807 0.7789 -0.3491  0.2617\ninsurance_public         1.1231   0.7752  1.4488 0.1474 -0.3962  2.6425\nace_score                0.0600   0.1419  0.4225 0.6727 -0.2182  0.3382\nhad_restraints           0.4735   0.1805  2.6230 0.0087  0.1197  0.8274\nlos_days                -0.0872   0.0826 -1.0557 0.2911 -0.2491  0.0747\nn_dsm5_categories        0.2650   0.3681  0.7199 0.4716 -0.4564  0.9864\nhas_medical_comorbidity  0.4892   0.1667  2.9337 0.0033  0.1624  0.8160\nhas_nssi                -0.2190   0.1976 -1.1083 0.2677 -0.6064  0.1683\nhas_trauma               0.1987   0.3108  0.6393 0.5226 -0